# The web build only needs: web/, packages/ (for @quittance/engine), the
# program's IDL-adjacent source (not its build output), evidence/, and the
# workspace root files pnpm needs to install. Everything else here is for the
# Android app, the devnet harness, or local tooling and would just blow past
# Vercel's 100MB-per-file / upload-size limits for no reason.
#
# Every pattern below is anchored with a leading slash where it names a
# repo-root directory or file. An unanchored "app/" previously matched
# web/app/ too — the Next.js App Router directory — which silently excluded
# it from the upload and left Vercel building an empty shell with no routes.

/app/
/probe/
/reference/
/docs/
/QUITTANCE_BUILD_INSTRUCTION.md
/ARCHITECTURE.md
/EVIDENCE.md
/LIMITATIONS.md
/MILESTONES.md
/PROGRESS.md
/README.md
/SECURITY.md
/TASK.md

/.anchor-build.err
/.anchor-build.log
/.anchor-install.err
/.anchor-install.log
/.sbf-install.err
/.sbf-install.log
/.cache/
/.keys/
/.git/

/program/
/target/

**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.turbo/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/dist/
**/build/
**/coverage/

web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
web/blob-report/
web/tests/
